<SharpAlertSource>FEMA IPAWS (WEA)</SharpAlertSource><alert xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:emergency:cap:1.2"><identifier>v2-3.13.6-1548469-1790371153066</identifier><sender>bsamson@lincolncountynm.gov</sender><sent>2026-09-25T22:19:13+01:00</sent><status>Actual</status><msgType>Update</msgType><source>070401 v3.13</source><scope>Public</scope><code>IPAWSv1.0</code><references>bsamson@lincolncountynm.gov,v2-3.13.6-1548455-1790370786987,2026-09-25T22:13:07+01:00</references><incidents>incidents</incidents><info><language>en-US</language><category>Met</category><event>Local Area Emergency</event><responseType>Evacuate</responseType><urgency>Immediate</urgency><severity>Extreme</severity><certainty>Observed</certainty><eventCode><valueName>SAME</valueName><value>LAE</value></eventCode><effective>2026-09-25T22:19:13+01:00</effective><expires>2026-09-26T01:19:13+01:00</expires><senderName>Public Alert System</senderName><headline>On Going Flash Flooding</headline><description>Ongoing flooding continues across portions of Lincoln County, and additional rainfall overnight may cause conditions to worsen. If you are in a low-lying or flood-prone area, near a drainage, arroyo, creek, or burn scar, MOVE TO HIGHER GROUND NOW. An evacuation and reunification center is open at Hondo Valley Public Schools, 111 Don Pablo Lane, Hondo. Do not cross flooded roadways. For information, call 575-336-8600.</description><instruction>Ongoing flooding continues in Lincoln County. Additional rainfall overnight may worsen conditions. If you are in a low-lying or flood-prone area, near a drainage, arroyo, creek, or burn scar, MOVE TO HIGHER GROUND NOW. An evacuation center is open at Hondo Schools. Do not cross flooded roads.</instruction><parameter><valueName>CMAMtext</valueName><value>On Going Flash Flooding Move to Higher Ground</value></parameter><parameter><valueName>CMAMlongtext</valueName><value>Ongoing flooding continues in Lincoln County. Additional rainfall overnight may worsen conditions.